          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BCP457 Granada POW Camp

Posted: N53° 36.895 W115° 22.497

My GPSr: N53° 36.895 W115° 22.496&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;(FOUND) GeoGuider and I headed west to see if we log as 'Found' a few brass caps (hoping the loophole for using GSAK was still open). Unfortunately the loophole is closed.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Didn't have time to see the POW camp location, but perhaps another time. Cap in good condition; thanks for the cap OFTH. Pictures to follow.&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="687751694">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-05-21T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Write note</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="1095439">GeoGuider</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP457 Granada POW Camp

Posted:  N53° 36.895  W115° 22.497

My GPSr:  N53° 36.895  W115° 22.496&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;j0ckser and I thought we'd travel west for the long weekend and see if we could pick up a few brass caps along the way.  I thought this was a very interesting spot as my dad was a guard at the POW camp in Lethbridge during WWII.  Thanks for the cap OFTH.

Pictures to follow&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
